	"$overlay-note": "The sources this build rebuilds replace their v0.8.18-retention-overlay files in an overlay on that corpus, and seven sources are new. Each rebuilt source takes the fixes since its files were built (v0.8.10-rebuild on 2026-11-02, the WOF samples of v0.8.6, geonames-features of v0.8.12): the line-break augmentation every synthesized row may take (#2992), the unit splitter's leading-type, grid-number and number-free-unit rules (#3025), the component check's enforced `postcode:repeats-region` rule, NAD read from release 24 with its placeholder spellings absent and its repeated unit parts dropped (#2895), the Texas notary city, suite and repeated-street fixes (#2895), and the 8,285 GNIS populated places in the WOF forks (#3061; whosonfirst-data-admin-us at 3f81e25abc8). `usgov-usgs-structures`, `fr-laposte-poincont` and `nc-opt-agences` are new, and so are four public-body registers first added as evaluation sources: `es-sanidad-centros-ap`, `it-miur-scuole`, `au-acnc-register` and `nz-charities-register`, each written by `heldout/fresh/build.run.ts`'s fetch under the cache root. Every other v0.8.18 source, the recipe outputs and the osm, overture and country-gap adapter sources, is carried unchanged.",
	"$street-index-note": "Every adapter that splits a trailing unit reads the street index built from v0.8.18-retention-overlay's premise-register rows, so no row attests itself.",
